   "search_text": "4. Let 𝑁be a positive integer and let (𝑘𝑛)𝑛≥1 be a sequence of positive integers with all terms\n   at most 𝑁. Annabel begins by choosing integers 𝑥1, 𝑥2, . . . , 𝑥𝑁. She then extends this to an\n   infinite sequence (𝑥𝑛)𝑛≥1 of integers by defining\n\n                                                𝑛−1\n                            𝑥𝑛= ∑︁  𝑥𝑖\n                                                  𝑖=𝑛−𝑘𝑛\n\n   for each 𝑛> 𝑁.\n\n  Show that there are either finitely many strictly positive terms or finitely many strictly\n   negative terms in the infinite sequence (𝑥𝑛).\n",
